<title>UK: UK Connex train drivers suspend overtime ban - BBC.</title>
<headline>UK Connex train drivers suspend overtime ban - BBC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Train drivers for southeast England regional operator Connex, part of Cie Generale des Eaux, have lifted their ban on overtime work, the BBC quoted their union ASLEF as saying on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The ban, imposed in protest at proposed changes to drivers' working practices, was lifted after new talks between ASLEF and Connex management. It will end at midnight on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The protest had affected one in five of Connex's Services into London from southeast England since it began on June 5.</p>
</text>
